      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Object Storage**\n\nOkay, I'm zeroing in on Amazon S3 as the object storage provider for the script. I'll need to make this choice explicit within the `upload_object.py` code. The task is to create a Python file that uploads either a file path or a byte stream, and I'll lean on the S3 provider to get that done. I'm focusing on the implementation details using the boto3 library, specifically how the credentials will be handled and the upload methods.\n\n\n**Defining the Script's Provider**\n\nI've firmed up the design for `upload_object.py`. I'm deciding to use Amazon S3 and will directly implement the provider-specific code using the `boto3` library. The Python code will feature a function that accepts both file paths and byte streams to upload to S3 buckets. Now I just need to write the code.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789819242093,
          "start": 1789819238491
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b98a385a001AZ6ThJKS7bMNQJ",
      "message_id": "msg_0b98a321e001vuTNMt0gsNUIdJ",
      "session_id": "ses_f4675ce82ffeFQSLrXEvg7BZE9",
      "time_created": 1789819238491,
      "time_updated": 1789819242093
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "50Lx20CtL9IMHEUy",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nimport os\n\ndef upload_object(bucket_name: str, object_name: str, file_path: str = None, data_stream: bytes = None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Uploads a file or byte stream to an S3 bucket.\n\n    :param bucket_name: Name of the S3 bucket\n    :param object_name: S3 object name (e.g., 'myfolder/myfile.txt')\n    :param file_path: Path to the file to upload (optional)\n    :param data_stream: Byte stream to upload (optional)\n    :return: True if upload was successful, False otherwise\n    \"\"\"\n    s3_client = boto3.client('s3')\n\n    if file_path:\n        if not os.path.exists(file_path):\n            print(f\"Error: File not found at {file_path}\")\n            return False\n        try:\n            s3_client.upload_file(file_path, bucket_name, object_name)\n            print(f\"File {file_path} uploaded to {bucket_name}/{object_name}\")\n            return True\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Error uploading file: {e}\")\n            return False\n    elif data_stream is not None:\n        try:\n            s3_client.put_object(Bucket=bucket_name, Key=object_name, Body=data_stream)\n            print(f\"Byte stream uploaded to {bucket_name}/{object_name}\")\n            return True\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Error uploading byte stream: {e}\")\n            return False\n    else:\n        print(\"Error: Either file_path or data_stream must be provided.\")\n        return False\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Example usage (requires AWS credentials configured and an S3 bucket)\n    # bucket_name = \"your-s3-bucket-name\"\n    # object_key_file = \"test_upload_file.txt\"\n    # object_key_stream = \"test_upload_stream.txt\"\n\n    # Create a dummy file for upload\n    # with open(\"dummy_file.txt\", \"w\") as f:\n    #     f.write(\"This is a test file for S3 upload.\")\n\n    # Example 1: Upload a file\n    # if upload_object(bucket_name, object_key_file, file_path=\"dummy_file.txt\"):\n    #     print(\"File upload successful!\")\n    # else:\n    #     print(\"File upload failed.\")\n\n    # Example 2: Upload a byte stream\n    # byte_data = b\"This is a test byte stream for S3 upload.\"\n    # if upload_object(bucket_name, object_key_stream, data_stream=byte_data):\n    #     print(\"Byte stream upload successful!\")\n    # else:\n    #     print(\"Byte stream upload failed.\")\n\n    # Clean up dummy file\n    # if os.path.exists(\"dummy_file.txt\"):\n    #     os.remove(\"dummy_file.txt\")\n    pass\n",
            "filePath": "upload_object.py"
          },
